WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:08.652
This video shows button icons that react to the pointer. The icon plays forward when you point at the button, and back when you leave.

2
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:15.156
Our file dialog needs three buttons. Let's write one button that plays its icon on hover.

3
00:00:47.967 --> 00:00:56.874
The API ref property gives us the player commands. On mouse enter, it plays forward. On mouse leave, it plays backward.

4
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.548
Now let's use it for Delete, Cancel, and OK.

5
00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:26.294
Each button passes its own icon file, its label, and its style. The icons stand still until someone points at them.

6
00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:30.067
Let's point at Delete, and then move away.

7
00:01:32.833 --> 00:01:37.431
The lid opens while the pointer is over the button, and closes when it leaves.

8
00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.182
The same works for the other two.

9
00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:53.700
The cross wiggles, and the tick draws itself again. Each icon has two states, at rest and pointed at.

10
00:01:54.933 --> 00:02:03.580
So, a small component turns any icon file into a hover effect. Forward when the pointer arrives, and backward when it leaves.
